class Solution {
    public int maxArea(int[] height) {
        // Two pointers: one at the start, one at the end
        int left=0;
        int right=height.length-1;

        int maxarea=0;
        while(left<right){
            // Calculate the area formed by the two lines
            int width=right-left;
            int minheight = Math.min(height[left], height[right]);
            int area=width*minheight;

            // Update maxArea if this area is larger
            maxarea=Math.max(maxarea, area);

            // Move the pointer pointing to the shorter line inward because moving the taller line won't help increase area
            if(height[left]<height[right]){
                left++;
            }else{
                right--;
            }
        }
        return maxarea;
    }
}



Time Complexity: O(n) (each pointer moves at most once across the array).
Space Complexity: O(1) (just variables).
